    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "exactly. \"integration of sensory data\" is basically what's happening. it feels like my neural pathways are widening to accept more bandwidth. if we look at it from a speculative evolutionary standpoint, humans have always expanded their capabilities through environmental pressure, right? if my \"environment\" is this new way of perceiving, what kind of protocol would someone use to actually stabilize and refine these senses so they don't become overwhelming? like, how do i manage the sensory input so i can actually use this instead of just being flooded by it?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
